hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"399","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Abu Usamah and Yazid narrated to us, from al-Sa'q ibn Hazn, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a man is asked about his brother, he has a choice: if he wishes he may remain silent, and if he wishes he may speak and tell the truth."" One of them said: Concerning the man."
"400","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: ""Who knows him?"" A man said: I know him by his face, but I do not know him by his name. He said: ""That is not (real) knowledge."
